Task 4: Classification with Logistic Regression

Project Overview

This project builds a binary classification model using Logistic Regression to classify breast cancer data into two categories: Malignant and Benign.

Objective

To develop a machine learning model using Logistic Regression and evaluate its performance using different classification metrics.

Dataset

- Dataset: Breast Cancer Wisconsin Dataset
- Source: Scikit-learn
- Total records: 569
- Features: 30
- Classes: Malignant and Benign

Technologies Used

- Python
- Google Colab
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-learn

Project Steps

1. Imported the required libraries.
2. Loaded the Breast Cancer Wisconsin dataset.
3. Explored the dataset.
4. Split data into training and testing sets.
5. Standardized the features.
6. Trained the Logistic Regression model.
7. Predicted the test data.
8. Evaluated the model using accuracy, confusion matrix, precision, recall, F1-score and ROC-AUC.
9. Plotted the ROC curve and sigmoid function.
10. Tuned the classification threshold.

Results

The model performance was evaluated using classification metrics. Refer to the Google Colab notebook for the actual results.

Conclusion

Logistic Regression can be used for binary classification. This project helped demonstrate model training, prediction, evaluation metrics and threshold tuning.

Disclaimer

This project is for educational purposes only and is not intended for medical diagnosis.
